scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (closes D-043). NEW `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested output; reads `output/scorecards/index.json` → `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`). Aggregator workflow extended (commit job invokes generator + adds markdown to operator-review PR). NEW MCP method `consult_scorecard` in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py` with read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, NEVER waiver content per invariant 2). NEW `tests/scorecard-report/` (3 golden fixtures × 2 tests = 7) + `tests/scp_mcp/test_tools/test_consult_scorecard.py` (9 tests including waiver-content scan). NEW ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 — adopter onboarding workflow (opt-in PR, privacy contract, MCP usage, 4 common failure modes table). 51/51 pytest pass. Internal-only delta to aggregator workflow; MCP method addition is additive (registered tool name only) so no federation primitive version bump per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\". |\n118:| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\n119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\n123:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\n137:**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\n141:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\n167:| WP-SCP-023 Threshold A operator sign-off — `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` lands as `not-yet-signed` at slice 023E; signs when ≥3 adopters opted in + ≥1 weekly aggregator clean. Operator-driven; no fixed date. | tbd | docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md |\n172:- ~~**TF-006**~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020Q** (this PR) — `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` gains Python-side mirrors of `policies/scp_common.rego` suppression helpers (`_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`, `_parse_dateish_ns`); `_run_opa` detects sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` and passes via `--data`; 5 new fixtures land — SCP-R-001/{waiver-suppressed, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled} + SCP-R-002/waiver-suppressed + SCP-R-004/waiver-suppressed. All 11 fixtures pass; both engines agree on every code path. Finding-id-level matching deferred to WP-SCP-023 per scp_common.rego comment. Closes the WP-SCP-023 prerequisite gate.\n187:- **TF-020H3-004**: §12.7.4 path examples (`services.yml`, `output/findings/waivers.json`, `policies/**`) are SCP-internal naming (was R1 completeness COMP-NIT-001). Estate-cascade adopters (FLA, PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower per WP-SCP-024) may have different file-shape conventions; v1.1 §12.7 wording could generalise. No deadline (cosmetic).\n193:- **TF-020H1-002**: `canary-replay.yml` paging rotation — at v1.0.0 the auto-opened `rule-regression` issue assigns `@jrnb2024` only (single-operator per D-031). For estate cascade (WP-SCP-024) a paging rotation would replace the assignee-only signal. Closure path: revisit at WP-SCP-024 planning OR at the 2026-07-21 quarterly bus-factor review when a second maintainer onboards. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MAJ-002 closure.\n194:- **TF-020H1-003**: `auto-defer` GitHub Action for stale rule-proposals — currently a manual close + `defer` label step (per `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2). For estate scale (post-WP-SCP-024 cascade) when proposal volume warrants automation, a scheduled GH Action would close PRs with no approvals after the 48h window. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-004 closure.\n230:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-023 023A (plan-doc) + 023B (emitter) + 023C (aggregator)\n232:- **TF-023A-001** (low priority): R-023-01 k-anonymity mitigation framing clarification when WP-SCP-024 cascade slice begins. The plan-doc R-023-01 risk row references \"slice 024 introduces aggregator-side k-anonymity\"; tighten when WP-SCP-024 plan-doc lands. Forward-compat; opportunistic.\n233:- **TF-023A-002** (medium priority): Cross-repo notification (v1.2.0 release announcement to ACC / CT / mapp-estate-regression) — **re-deferred to slice 023E** (was 023D; 023D ships exposure surface but Threshold A onboarding is where adopters first participate). Until adopters can opt in with the exposure surface live, the notification is a \"pre-Threshold-A FYI\" only. Filed at WP-SCP-023 023A; re-deferred at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-001.\n250:- **TF-023E-002** (medium priority): SCP-self wrapper SHA pin is **stuck at v1.0.0 (@41a5299)** — bumping to any post-WP-SCP-023 SHA produces `startup_failure` because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation) against the caller's ceiling. The `attest-scorecard` job in `policy-check.yml@5ff2acd` declares `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`, which exceeds the wrapper's `contents:read + statuses:write` ceiling, even when `scorecard-emit: false` would skip the job at runtime. Closure path: (a) restructure `policy-check.yml` so `attest-scorecard` lives in a separate top-level workflow file (called workflows can't have job-scoped perms above caller ceiling regardless of `if:`), OR (b) once TF-023E-001 unblocks (repo public/org-owned), grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` universally at the wrapper level. (a) preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters and is the recommended path. Surfaced at 023E fix-round-3 (the bumped wrapper failed startup_failure even after reverting `scorecard-emit: true` because the SHA bump alone trips the validation). Real adopters that opt in MUST follow the (b) path because they will universally grant the two permissions per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2.\n258:## Recent decisions\n272:- **D-041 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B. MAJOR-pinned schema; default-false `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input; OIDC artifact attestation via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0`; aggregator verifies at slice 023C via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema's `additionalProperties: false`). v1.1.0 → v1.2.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). Closes plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation.\n273:- **D-042 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C. Per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint pre-committed at 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits + CODEOWNERS + branch protection (NOT a separate Ed25519 layer; Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub). Two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) mirrors 023B's `attest-scorecard` job pattern. Internal-only; no semver bump. Closes plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation.\n274:- **D-043 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D. Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested). MCP method has read-only contract per plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, never waiver content per invariant 2; Pydantic-enforced field whitelist). ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. Closes plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation.\n293:- **WP-SCP-023**: cross-repo scorecards.\n294:- **WP-SCP-024**: estate cascade (FLA pilot → PIM/recommender/etc.).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
